{"assets":["/statement-assets/7d37f61543e19896584977ca7eb50f40cd3f5fdc8a0fc2c15cc90f88f43a1160.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"696","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Puzzles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Barney lives in country USC (United States of Charzeh). USC has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" roads between them. Cities and roads of USC form a rooted tree (Barney's not sure why it is rooted). Root of the tree is the city number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus if one will start his journey from city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", he can visit any city he wants by following roads."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7d37f61543e19896584977ca7eb50f40cd3f5fdc8a0fc2c15cc90f88f43a1160.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Some girl has stolen Barney's heart, and Barney wants to find her. He starts looking for in the root of the tree and (since he is Barney Stinson not a random guy), he uses a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"random DFS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to search in the cities. A pseudo code of this algorithm is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nlet starting_time be an array of length n\ncurrent_time = 0\ndfs(v):\n\tcurrent_time = current_time + 1\n\tstarting_time[v] = current_time\n\tshuffle children[v] randomly (each permutation with equal possibility)\n\t// children[v] is vector of children cities of city v\n\tfor u in children[v]:\n\t\tdfs(u)\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As told before, Barney will start his journey in the root of the tree (equivalent to call "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dfs(1)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Barney needs to pack a backpack and so he wants to know more about his upcoming journey: for every city "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":", Barney wants to know the expected value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"starting_time[i]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". He's a friend of Jon Snow and knows nothing, that's why he asked for your help."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of cities in USC."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p2, p3, ..., pn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ pi < i"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of the parent city of city number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the tree, meaning there is a road between cities numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" in USC."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first and only line of output print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th number is the expected value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"starting_time[i]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your answer for each city will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\n1 2 1 1 4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.0 4.0 5.0 3.5 4.5 5.0 5.0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n1 1 2 2 4 4 3 3 1 10 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.0 5.0 5.5 6.5 7.5 8.0 8.0 7.0 7.5 6.5 7.5 8.0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"696B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/696/problem/B"}